mu4e-autotask NEWS -- history of user-visible changes

* Changes in mu4e-autotask 1.1.0 (unreleased)

** Incompatible Changes

*** mu4e 1.12.5 or later is required
    The stated requirement was mu4e 1.12, but RSVP replies use
    `mu4e-compose-reply-to', added in 1.12.5.

*** Compose hooks of `mu4e-autotask-send-email' see no `mu4e-contexts'
    Hooks that run while the template's message is composed, such as
    `mu4e-compose-pre-hook' and `mu4e-compose-mode-hook', see no
    contexts, so one that switches context signals "No contexts
    defined".  `mu4e-context-current' is the template's context there.

*** Recording an event leaves the event file unsaved
    Recording an event saved the event file, and was refused when a
    buffer visiting it had unsaved changes.  org-gcal edits the entry
    it posts without saving, so the next event recorded into the file
    in the session was refused, after its RSVP had been sent.  The
    entry is now appended to the file's buffer and left unsaved there,
    as org-gcal leaves its own edits.  Recording is refused, after the
    RSVP has been sent, while an org-capture into the file is open, as
    aborting that capture can delete the entry.

** New Features

*** New action helper `mu4e-autotask-browse-html-url-matching'
    Browses and returns the URL captured by REGEXP in the current
    message's text/html body, decoded from its transfer encoding and
    its Content-Type charset as remapped by `mm-charset-override-alist'
    (UTF-8 if that charset is absent, us-ascii or unknown) so that
    REGEXP can contain non-ASCII text.  Signals a `user-error' when the
    message has no HTML part.

** Bug Fixes

*** `mu4e-autotask-browse-url-matching' decodes more character references
    Besides `&amp;', the captured URL now has `;'-terminated decimal
    and hexadecimal HTML character references, `&lt;', `&gt;',
    `&quot;' and `&apos;', and the uppercase `&AMP;', `&LT;', `&GT;'
    and `&QUOT;' decoded, in a single pass.  An href such as
    "pay?id&#x3D;7" used to be browsed with the reference intact.
    Tabs, and CR and LF decoded from references, are then removed, as
    a browser does.

*** Invitations without SUMMARY can be answered on Emacs 31
    Accepting, declining or tentatively accepting a calendar
    invitation that has no SUMMARY used to fail on Emacs 31 with a
    wrong-type-argument error from the Gnus reply builder.

*** RSVP replies with non-ASCII text are sent in UTF-8
    The reply's calendar part named its UTF-8 charset inside the MIME
    type, so the message encoder added a second charset parameter and
    encoded the part in the charset it preferred, such as ISO-2022-JP
    in a Japanese language environment.

*** Send success functions run at most once
    A sent compose buffer is only buried, keeping the hook that calls
    the success function of `mu4e-autotask-send-email' and
    `mu4e-autotask-do-send-email', so resending from it called that
    function again: an RSVP warned that the event file had unsaved
    changes, or recorded its event a second time.

*** `mu4e-autotask-send-email' keeps the template's context
    A mu4e context whose match function accepts the nil parent of a
    new message, such as one that matches by host name or time of day,
    took over the message composed from the template: its From
    address, signature and folders replaced the template context's.

*** Sent messages are signed or encrypted whole under a crypto policy
    mu4e puts the <#secure> tag that `mu4e-compose-crypto-policy' asks
    for at the top of a composed message's body, and mml signs or
    encrypts only what follows the tag.  RSVP replies and
    `mu4e-autotask-send-email' inserted their parts above it, so under
    a signing policy they went out unsigned, and under an encrypting
    one Message asked whether to send them unencrypted.  A message
    from a template also showed the tag as text after its body, unless
    an attachment came between them; then, as in an RSVP reply, the
    tag became an extra signed or encrypted part that was empty or
    held only the signature.  RSVP replies and
    `mu4e-autotask-send-email' now insert their parts after the tag.

*** Template bodies end their line
    A template body that did not end in a line break ran into the text
    after it: a compose hook's text at the top of the body, or the
    signature separator when `message-signature-insert-empty-line' is
    nil.  `mu4e-autotask-send-email' now ends the body's last line, so
    by default such a body gets the empty line before the signature
    that one ending in a line break already got.

* Changes in mu4e-autotask 1.0.0 (2026-08-21)

Initial release.
